From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000004 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CEB-GNRD platform <ceb-gnrd@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: pmbus: rate-limit unavailable status-register warning

Optional hot-plug PSU addresses may disappear during probe. Keep the probe
failure and its -ENODEV result unchanged, but record the diagnostic as a
rate-limited warning. The board's console policy retains warnings in the
kernel ring buffer without printing them over serial login input.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board console policy]
---
diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/pmbus/pmbus_core.c b/drivers/hwmon/pmbus/pmbus_core.c
--- a/drivers/hwmon/pmbus/pmbus_core.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/pmbus/pmbus_core.c
@@ -2756,4 +2756,4 @@
 		if (ret < 0 || ret == 0xff) {
-			dev_err(dev, "PMBus status register not found\n");
+			dev_warn_ratelimited(dev, "PMBus status register not found\n");
 			return -ENODEV;
 		}
-- 
2.47.0
